module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.generic_match_field_binding_keeps_its_type_parameter

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data generic_match_field_binding_keeps_its_type_parameter: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "generic_match_field_binding_keeps_its_type_parameter" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "SPECIMEN CLASS, 2026-11-15 (merry-fox-617, taking over crisp-dove-701, PR 16520; node native-emit-match-binding-keeps-its-type; purpose v2 self-host/native closure qualification under gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing). A `match` that binds a variant FIELD out of a GENERIC enum and crosses that binding with `as` lowered the binding to compile_error!(UNRESOLVED_CompilerError) at NATIVE EMIT, while typecheck and interpretation both ACCEPTED the program. Minimal reproduction: `fn use_c(p: Optional<NonEmptyStr>) -> String { match p { Absent {} => \"none\"  Present { value: v } => v as String } }`. The bound field's resolved type still named the enum's type parameter T instead of the scrutinee's concrete argument, so the emitter (whose read-node.inferred contract is correct and was NOT special-cased) had no type to cross and emitted the refusal. A non-generic enum with the identical binding shape emitted correctly throughout, which pins the defect to generic-enum field bindings and excludes arm order, fn-return and match binding in general.",
    "EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY (gunbc.design_argument::earliest_unjustified_boundary, gunbc.design_argument::single_authority): the kernel MINT of the generic coproduct, v1.compiler.infer_types kernel_optional_type_node, is a hand-built second spelling of `type Optional<T> = Absent | Present { value: T }`. It was spelled with params: [] and Present.value.inferred = TypeVariable { present_value }, decoupled from the declaration. Because the mint carried no parameter, v1.compiler.infer_patterns generic_use_slot_bindings built an EMPTY slot map at every use site, so the matched Present.value field kept its unbound payload node and was never rewritten to the concrete argument. The mint was the one node violating the shape that v1.compiler.infer_types kernel_optional_shape_refusal already ENFORCES of every Optional declaration (params count 1, payload field typed by the parameter). The defect surfaced only at emit because typecheck and interpretation never read the static field type; the emitter does. It could not be DERIVED from the std.optional declaration: the kernel type environment is the seed that typechecks std.optional itself, so reading that declaration is circular. Repair: make the mint carry the declaration's parameter -- add the T parameter to params, type Present.value by it -- so generic_use_slot_bindings resolves the slot, AND substitute the use-site argument into each variant field's Resolved { node } in v1.compiler.infer_patterns expand_scrut_type_for_variant_lookup (the existing substitute_type_slots_scoped cannot reach a field's Resolved { node } because the field leaf is not itself a slot key and resolved_slots is false).",
    "CONTROL (test.claim.emitter_generic_match_field_binding_witness, hook compile_dag_rust_emit_check which lives in the test home, not in gunbc.roadmap): two generic controls bind Present.value out of an Optional<NonEmptyStr> crossed with `as`, from a parameter-typed scrutinee and from an fn-returned scrutinee -- the distinct acquisition paths the defect was bisected across -- asserting the realized cast and forbidding compile_error!; these are RED on the unfixed seed (the refusal renders compile_error!) and GREEN after the fix. Control G binds a NON-generic enum field and crosses it with `as`; it emits on both sides and is the negative control pinning the generic-specificity. This row claims NO rung increase: fleet regeneration and execution against the base binary remain pending.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
